From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:41:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gui: key-replace's scroll check reads positions, not the
 .holds marker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Since d74ef5e04 (an inner list keeps the wheel) app.js marks a scrolled
box .holds on pointerover and wheel, and this file's scrolled() reader
folded that marker into its string. At 420px, sc was read while the
editor's body was marked; then the replace's answer re-rendered the
dialog — openModal builds a fresh body and puts its scrollTop back, the
marker it does not — and the assertion read the fresh body before the
engine's next hover pass had marked it again: "changing the key
scrolled", '0 ebody:200' against '0 ebody holds:200', though nothing had
scrolled. WebKit loses that race on an idle machine: 9 of 10 runs of the
file's ten webkit cases went red this way here, and 6104e88aa's four
webkit 420px reds under load are the same strings. It is not a 5s action
limit, so the 15s room (the commit before) doesn't cover it.

The reader now takes positions only — the page's scrollY and each
scrolled box's scrollTop — which is what "nothing scrolls" asserts. The
marker is pointer-proximity state by design (gui-shell.md), not layout;
the wheel-containment feature itself is untouched.

Run (playwright 1.57.0, idle machine):
- webkit before: 4 of 5 languages at 420px red, then 5 of 5; every red
  is 'changing the key scrolled', actual '0 ebody:200', expected
  '0 ebody holds:200'; chromium 20/20 green
- webkit after: 20/20 twice; chromium: 20/20
- the reader reverted alone: webkit red 5 of 5 with the same strings;
  restored: 20/20
- adjacent, untouched: key-import 12/12, inner-scroll-contain 44/44
  (both engines each)

Siblings: the same composite reader is in some twenty more specs
(key-import, key-plan, key-copy, key-weight, rest-try-now,
provider-many-keys, account-*, model-*, by-agent and the skill/project
files). One goes red only where its own capture-to-compare straddles a
re-render of a marked scrolled box; only key-replace has an observed
red, so it alone changes, as routing-scroll-end alone did in d74ef5e04.

Fixes #3476

